      "value": "@{5fcd676570b59138e6ef0271|full_name}I agree with Rat, I feel this is actually a thing that needs patched in the VRCSDK itself instead.\n\nAlso a few changes I feel that can be useful to many to limit their audio sources to 1 for this:\n\n- allow loop to be set per clip instead, this would help simplify things for when people want to mix some looped clips and non-looped ones together.\n\n- a setting per clip that says \"this is an additive clip that plays on with any other clip\" (could be a looped one). Many old games even PlayStation 1 games back in 1996~early 2000's had additive clip features to make their games more realistic and was not much of a performance killer (look at Crash Bandicoot for example with additive textures and speech/sound chunks in their nsd/nsf files). Basically what additive sounds do is blend with the looped clips for the duration of the additive sound before it returns to the normal looped clip (simulates multiple audio sources without having multiple).\n\nAdding these 2 things can allow many people who have avatars that need both looped and non-looped clips and also need to use only a single Audio source to be possible without negatively affecting performance in VRChat because of it. Also such a change is more sane to do as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
